Content: the hang monitor and the embedder's own DevTools clients.

WebContentsImpl::ShouldIgnoreUnresponsiveRenderer() drops every hang report
while any DevTools client is attached to the page, since the renderer may sit
on a breakpoint. zebkit drives its own views through a DevTools session of
their own (evaluation, init scripts, grants), which never pauses a page: with
it attached, WebContentsDelegate::RendererUnresponsive() was never called and
zebkit_view_on_responsiveness() could not work. SetDebuggerAttachedForHangs()
(content/public/browser/zebkit_hang_monitor.h) lets the embedder answer
instead; zebkit counts every client but a view's own, so an external
debugger, a Playwright client and DevTools still hold the monitor, as in
Chrome. A function in a new header rather than a ContentBrowserClient or
WebContentsDelegate method, which nearly all of content would be rebuilt for.

